# Eco-Wizard

## Lore

The Eco-Wizard is a barbarian sorcerer of Dinosaur Swamp who works magic into weapons and tools carved from the region''s own materials: wood, bone, teeth, hide, sinew and plant fiber. The practice grew up among the tribes after the Great Cataclysm, when a few learned that ley line energy could be channeled into crafted things as well as through themselves. As mutation spread psychic ability through the tribes, more people could wield those items, and their makers rose in standing.

They are often compared to Techno-Wizards working in organic parts rather than wire and crystal. They have nothing to do with Necromancy or Bio-Wizardry, enslave no spirits and deal with no demons. Like most barbarians they treat nature as friend, enemy and resource at once: they neither revere it nor waste it, and do not kill without need.

## GM Notes

Eco-Wizard items are the EW gear rows of this book (printed 83-95). A starting character typically wears hide armor with two or three magic features of the player''s choice (Chameleon, Shadow Meld, Repel Animals and Cleanse are favorites) and carries one weapon per W.P., at least one of them enchanted; Sickness Spears and Skin Nets are common. At the G.M.''s discretion, the player may craft one or two unique weapons to start with; a lost or broken one needs the right spells or a return to the teacher to replace.

Starting kit beyond the sheet: 1D6 feet of sinew, a collection of leg bones and a patch of leather hide for building constructs.

Eco-Wizards prefer organic weapons, avoid ordinary technology and, on philosophical grounds, Techno-Wizard devices (which they can use), and find Bio-Wizard creations cruel. They travel on foot and rely on companions for long journeys.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'eco-wizard');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'eco-wizard';

